# Zong blockade of Daras — internal notes

## Scribe notes
- Standalone Daras history article.
- Covers the 1907–1911 blockade imposed by Zong after the Darasian Socialist Revolution.
- Main political purpose: show of force, economic pressure, and containment of socialist influence in Fosia.
- Settlement terms need to stay explicit: transit restored, navy construction limited, passage fees continued until 1925.
- This article should reconcile the existing Darasian Socialist Revolution page, which currently frames the blockade too broadly.

## Open questions
- Whether the memorandum should be named formally or left anonymous as a memorandum of understanding.
- Whether the wording "free transit" should be interpreted as unrestricted transit rights or merely restored transit rights subject to passage fees.
- Whether any additional Daras or Zong history pages should mention the blockade beyond the two pages already identified.

